A||||5||FieroPerformance||How much HP with these upgrades?||||5||
Z||000000||FieroPerformance||06-27-2001||04:22 PM||||Hey,<P>     I am playing with the idea of pulling my engine and doing some work on it. I was wondering how much hp to expect out of my 2.8 with the following mods.<P>This is what I am planning on doing:<BR>1. Performance rebuild with high compression pistons<BR>2. Roller rockers<BR>3. Cold air induction<BR>4. Underdrive pulley<BR>5. Exhaust headers<P>After this I am playing with the idea of running a 75 shot of nitrous but I want to get an idea of how much HP I will have without the nos first.<P>Thanks,<BR>-Charlie||||reg||5
Z||000001||AkursedX||06-27-2001||04:29 PM||||I would guess somewhere between 170-185hp at the flywheel.  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||06-27-2001||05:59 PM||||About 155 @ 5000 rpm and 191-ft. lbs. of torque @ 3500 rpm if you keep the same camshaft and use headers/high performance manifolds like the Sprint manifolds and a high flow muffler. I used a 9.5-1 compression ratio.<P>With a 75-shot of nitrous you will have 225 horsepower @ 5000 RPM and 336-ft. lbs. of torque @ 2500 rpm or 320 @ 3000 rpm.   <P>Add 6% for the pulley or 9 peak horsepower and 5 peak horsepower for rocker arms if they are like Crane Gold race rockers, full rocker bearing rockers.<P>The cold air induction I don't know. It depends on what you get. The stock unit is a cold air induction anyway.<P>If you want to make power than spend the money on the heads, camshaft, and a good set of headers like the FOCOA headers. Focus on the engine breathing.<P> <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierowrecker||06-27-2001||06:13 PM||||Hey back!<P>So are we talking 12:1 compression?<BR>How about a full race cam??<P>Seriously, if you are building up an engine, then you will plan on the outcome and not go on wild ass guesses...<P>I could throw numbers at you all day, but they don't have any relavence to what YOU do, and what you end up with...<BR>Talk to an engine builder in your area for tips and tricks, or call Summit Racing if you don't have a local builder...<BR>crash...<p>[This message has been edited by Fierowrecker (edited 06-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||06-27-2001||06:23 PM||||Always remember...If you paint your calipers yellow, you'll gain 15hp.  And each sticker is worth another 4hp (except for "Pontiac" stickers which are worth 9hp).<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000005||StuGood||06-27-2001||07:16 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B>Always remember...If you paint your calipers yellow, you'll gain 15hp...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>There's probably some truth to that yellow calipers rule... if you pull off the calipers to clean and paint them, you might free up brakes that had been dragging for the last 10k miles.  ||||reg||12
